The Junior Accounts Executive responsible to handle Accounts Payable (AP) activities, ensure accuracy and timely processing, follow policies and procedures or relevant regulations.
Main duties as follows:
Verification of invoices from vendors and arrange payments by due date;
Verification of staff expenses claims and arrange payments by due date;
Assist in petty cash management which includes timely replenishment of funds;
Assist in updating and maintaining the Fixed Assets Register;
Ensure accounting entries are posted into the finance operating system on time and accurately;
Ensure all accounting records and documents are properly filed, labeled and kept for future references/ audit checks;
Any other matters to be assigned from time to time by the superiors
Requirements:
LCCI / Diploma or Degree in Accounting or equivalent;
1-2 years of relevant accounting experience in the relevant position;
Computer literate with sound knowledge in usage of accounting software;
Advanced Excel skills;
Advanced Access skills;
Required language(s): English and Bahasa Malaysia;
Able to communicate to Managers, Colleagues and Suppliers confidently;
Able to work under pressure and to tight deadlines;
You’ll be a team player with willingness to help others beyond their formal role;
Detailed and consistent follow-up, able to multi-task and willing to learn.
This position will be based in our Kuala Lumpur office at Menara KH, Jalan Sultan Ismail, 50250.

Responsibilities:
Proactively monitor, detect and response to known and or emerging threats;
Create and maintain operational reports and dashboard;
Develop, update, and implement cybersecurity measures and controls;
Determine, adapt, and maintain corporate cybersecurity procedures and policies;
Collect and analyse threat intelligence and produce TI report to update various stakeholders;
Identify and prioritize vulnerabilities, working with IT teams to ensure timely remediation;
Perform diverse duties assigned by the manager to support organizational security goals and initiatives.
Requirements:
Diploma/Degree in Computer Science, IT Security, or a related field;
Possesses relevant professional certifications (e.g. CEH, CSX-P or CySA+);
0-3 years thorough knowledge and experience in Information Technology, fresh graduate is welcome to apply.
Working knowledge and exposure to any EPP, SIEM, DLP, EDR, WAF, PAM, CNAPP or any other security solutions;
Knowledge/experience with operating systems, networking technology and cybersecurity theory; Possessing knowledge of cloud security and PAM is advantageous
Familiarity with cyber security standard/framework (e.g. CIS Benchmark, NIST CSF, ISO 27001);
Familiarity with legal and regulatory standard/framework. (e.g. MAS TRMG, BNM RMiT, SG/MY PDPA);
Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;
Ability to deal with the ambiguity associated with working in a fast paced and changing environment.
Our offer:
Career development prospect;
Attractive remuneration package;
5-day working week;
21+ days Annual Leave;
Medical, Dental, Life Insurance;
Performance bonus and shares;
Staff discount on Securities Transaction
Training, sports allowance.
Perks & Benefits:
Fun:
Game room with PS4, FIFA19 and Foosball at all time.
Snacks & Beverages:
Vending machines with various snacks and drinks for you to choose. Coffee machine with fresh brew Expresso, Americano, Latte and many more at your choice. Weekly Fruits Day and Monthly Ice-cream day too!
Yearly activities:
Movie Day, Outdoor activities, Celebration during festive seasons and many more!
Investment:
0% sales charge* if you invest through our platform.
Remuneration package:
Competitive Salary (way above market rate if you the right potential!)
Coverage:
Insurance and medical coverage.
Allowances:
Monthly sports allowance, Yearly department gathering and welcome dinner for new staffs.
Annual Leaves:
21 days.
