To assist in training, performance management, HR budgeting, employee relations, industrial relations, employee wellbeing & etc.
Assists to drive talent management program to retain talents while maximize the talent capabilities via effective training program that may include mentoring & coaching, etc;
To assist in building a strong business relationship, facilitating the Implementation of key and effective HR initiatives and practices across RCE Group of Companies;
To assist in providing employees and managers with an available first point of contact for questions and guidance on fundamental HR topics and issues;
Work closely with management and employees to improve work relationships, build morale, and increase productivity and retention and act as change agent to drive application in enabling a performance culture and engaged workforce;
To assist to managing and resolving people issues by engaging relevant stakeholders and secure alignment and buy in;
Provide advice and counsel to managers and employees to ensure consistent application and integration of policies, procedures and practices at 100% compliance to promote an ethical and compliant work environment.
Job Requirements:
Candidates must possess at least a degree in Human Resources or any equivalent background;
Preferably candidate with 1 or more years of relevant HR experience;
Good interpersonal skills, analytics skills, strong written and oral communication skills and the ability to multi-task in a fast paced environment;
Fast learner and a good team player;
Proficient in MS Office application likes Microsoft Excel and Microsoft Words;
Applicant(s) must be Malaysia citizen.

Prepare and ensure clients' monthly / yearly management accounts are completed accurately and on time;
Prepare ad-hoc financial management reports requested by Clients;
Liaise and follow-up with clients on any outstanding issues;
Liaise with clients' Auditor / Tax Agent;
Assist in filing of clients' documents;
Assist Supervisor on other admin tasks; &
Occasionally might need to travel to client site.
Accounting student looking for internship placement, please email us your resume or you may apply through this post just indicate that you are looking for an internship placement.
Job Requirements:
Candidate must possess relevant accounting qualification or currently pursuing professional accounting examinations;
Fresh graduate are welcome to apply;
Energetic and with analytical mind;
Problem solving skills;
Willing to work under pressure, tights deadline and over time.

To carry out project coordination, control system design, program developement, programming with Site Testing & Commissioning;
To develop PLC, SCADA, HMI mainly with SIEMENS, MITSUBISHI, OMRON brand;
To design electrical drawing for PLC Panel and Low Voltage MCC Starter Panel;
Requirements:
Candidate must possess at least Bachelor's Degree/Post Graduate Diploma/Professional Degree in Engineering (Mechatronic/Electromechanical), Engineering (Electrical/Electronic) or equivalent.
At least 1 Year(s) of working experience in the related field is required for this position.
Fresh Graduate encourages to apply
Required Skill(s): PLC, HMI, SCADA, AUTOCAD
Knowledgeable in Process Control Instrumentation, Electrical Installation works, MCC Panel Design, PLC, SCADA and HMI will be added advantage;
Willing to travel oversea & outstation and work long hours when required;
Preferably Junior or Senior Executive specialized in Engineering - Electrical or equivalent.
Result-driven, self motivated, positive working attitude and able to work independently to achieve targets;

Tasks & Responsibilities
Manage, oversee and work on daily operations of the accounting department;
Assist to produce, monitor and analyze accounting data and produce financial reports and statements;
Coordinate and assist in administrative, bank financing matters, tax planning, feasibility studies and financial modelling;
Improve systems and procedures including suggest for improvements;
Implement and maintain company's Management System (ISO 9001, ISO 14001 and ISO 45001).
Qualification Requirements
Candidate must possess at least Bachelor's Degree/Professional qualifications or currently pursuing final stage of professional examinations;
Familiar with local accounting and taxation requirements;
At least 1 year of working experience in the accounting field and able to handle full set accounts;
Experience in handling project accounting shall be an added advantage;
Committed, proactive, systematic, responsible and organized at work;
Good communication and interpersonal skills;
Proficient in using computer software like MS Excel, MS Word, etc.;
Required languages: English, Bahasa Malaysia.

We are hiring a FEW Account cum Admin Senior/Junior to join us to provide professional corporate compliance services-bookkeeping, admin support, human resource to our local & oversea clients .
Responsibilities:
Prepare banking online payments, KWSP, SOCSO, EIS, LHDN and HRDCorp payments;
Prepare immigration doc submissions;
Attending to various government departments;
Data entry and complete management account;
Communicate & liaise with clients on compliance matters.
Job Requirements:
Experienced & Fresh graduates are welcome;
Degree/Diploma in Accounting, Business Administration;
Working knowledge of UBS Accounting, UBS Payroll; SAP, SQL, Superior Tax;
Command of languages to liaise with clients from different nationalities - English/Bahasa/Mandarin.
Team player, pleasant personality, willing to handle different nature of tasks, versatile and adaptive, can work independently and meet deadlines;
Well-organised with strong attention to details.
Valid driving license.

1. Safety
Maintains a safe working environment at the assigned area by ensuring compliance with equipment/machine safety guidelines and reinforcing safety standard operating procedures in the production area;
Ensures that safety, GMP and hygiene are observed in his/her area;
Provide deeper analysis and report on ORS on the Safety Observations at his/her area;
Lead the LMRA before executing both routine and non-routine activities;
Follow ups the closure of the safety observations in his/her area;
Suggests improvements in safety and ergonomics in his/her area.
2.
Quality
Employ corrective and preventive actions on machines in case of deviation as documented in the Quality Plan;
Perform RCA for every deviation occurrence according to the RCA Triggering Matrix;
Partner with Quality on line release activities.
3. Service / Volume – Core Job
Perform SAP transactions for breakdown, corrective and preventive maintenance;
Perform machine and environment cleaning based on Hygiene standards after every Maintenance;
Perform troubleshooting of the equipment in the case of a breakdown;
Perform other duties as assigned by the immediate superior;
Basic trouble shooting/ First line maintenance;
Perform routine check-up of all running machines (e.g. belts, bolts, leaks, etc);
Perform breakdown maintenance of production equipment and its auxiliary components including CIP line;
Performed assigned maintenance checklist and performance physical preventive maintenance during plan shut downs
4. Process confirmation & continuous improvement
Ensure the standard way of working and provide analyses of current (work)processes, evaluate bottlenecks and advice regarding improvements, and ensure implementation after approval;
Pro-actively do machine inspections and find for abnormalities and escalate
Continuously look for improvement initiatives to optimize and standardize production processes.
Create an environment of continuous improvement by emphasizing the importance of improvement and by facilitating the team to identify opportunities;
Participate in CI projects, propose and implement on the machines
Participate in RCA meetings and conduct 1st line RCA during breakdown by collection technical information
Job Requirements:
Work and think level: Higher Vocational / Diploma in technical
Fresh graduate / at least 1 year relevant work experience
Technical Diploma in electrical/mechanical/automation
Interpersonal communication skills on all levels
Continuous improvement
Analytical skills
Prioritizing and decision making
Result-oriented and stress resistant

Aglow Medical Group is a trusted medical and aesthetic corporation that is constantly growing and expanding. We have within 3.5 years grown from 1 clinic to 20 clinics. Our team consists of a group of certified, trained and experienced medical doctors, corporate experts, passionate aestheticians and healthcare providers who are dedicated to providing specialized services to our clients.
In Aglow Clinic, it is our utmost duty to let everyone’s inner beauty shine through the enhancement of their external beauty. With medical grade aesthetic solutions for everyone in need - from head to toe, we deliver satisfying treatment results in an environment exuding elegant ambience, with unparalleled client service that focuses on having a genuine, effective and friendly approach.
We are looking for an energetic candidate to fulfill our vacancy for a
MIS Executive.
Job responsibilities:
To conduct system training for new staff members;
To create profiles for new staff and share login details with them;
To set up POS system for new clinic;
To ensure all staff are kept informed of new features and updates to the system.
To manage administrative responsibilities as the admin of the POS system;
To generate reports from the POS system;
To report any system errors to the vendor, closely monitor, and follow up on system updates;
To coordinate office activities and operations to ensure efficiency and compliance with company policies;
To assist with ad-hoc office or clinic activities;
To support in preparing regularly scheduled reports;
To submit and reconcile expense reports;
To handle commission calculations for all clinics.
Requirements:
Candidate must possess at least a Diploma / Advanced / Higher / Graduate Diploma in Information Management System and Business Management or equivalent.
Fresh graduates are encouraged to apply.
Strong communication, interpersonal & follow up skills
Required language (s) : English, Mandarin, Bahasa Malaysia. Knowledge in another language is advantages.
Experience with the KUMO System is an added advantage.
Strong analytical and leadership skills with keen attention to detail and resourcefulness.
1 Full-time position (s) available
Kindly contact to :
013-5041330
(WhatsApp)
Job Highlights
Parking pass will be provided.
Exclusive staff purchase discount.
Very Convenient Location, Nearby LRT Station & KTM station, Office is above shopping mall;
Provide opportunities for career advancement;
Vibrant and energetic office culture;
Performance is always rewarded accordingly.

